Keep frontend fetches and asset paths relative, such as `./api/status` and `./assets/app.js`, so links keep working inside AutoYou.

## Website security contract

For Python/FastAPI scaffolds, keep the generated `create_agent_website_app`
boundary in place for private agent data and controls. Its backend rejects
protected API requests with 401 until the assigned per-agent TOTP profile
succeeds, then falls back to the shared pairing TOTP when no profile is
assigned.

For Node/TypeScript, Go, and Rust scaffolds, the generated backend is a generic
local HTTP starter. Keep it free of private agent data until you add explicit
authentication for custom routes.
